Private modules should not hide a workspace library's CMJ metadata (#17020).

  $ make_melange_project 3.25 1.0
  $ mkdir lib app
  $ cat > lib/dune <<'EOF'
  > (library
  >  (name lib)
  >  (modes melange)
  >  (private_modules impl))
  > EOF
  $ echo 'let add3 a b c = a + b + c' > lib/impl.ml
  $ echo 'let add3 = Impl.add3' > lib/lib.ml
  $ cat > app/dune <<'EOF'
  > (melange.emit
  >  (target out)
  >  (emit_stdlib false)
  >  (libraries lib)
  >  (module_systems (esm js)))
  > EOF
  $ echo 'let () = Js.log (Lib.add3 1 2 3)' > app/main.ml

The consumer cannot find the CMJ metadata and uses a Curry call.

  $ dune build app/out/app/main.js
  $ cat _build/default/app/out/app/main.js
  // Generated by Melange
  
  import * as Curry from "melange.js/curry.js";
  import * as Lib from "../lib/lib.js";
  
  console.log(Curry._3(Lib.add3, 1, 2, 3));
  /*  Not a pure module */

Without private modules, the same consumer calls the implementation directly.

  $ cat > lib/dune <<'EOF'
  > (library
  >  (name lib)
  >  (modes melange))
  > EOF
  $ dune build app/out/app/main.js
  $ cat _build/default/app/out/app/main.js
  // Generated by Melange
  
  import * as Lib__Impl from "../lib/impl.js";
  
  console.log(Lib__Impl.add3(1, 2, 3));
  /*  Not a pure module */
